---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import IdentityRichText from '../components/IdentityRichText.astro';
import { umjcMembershipValue } from '../data/congregationIdentity';
---
<PageLayout title="UMJC Membership - Kehilat Ohr HaTorah" pageTitle="Our UMJC Membership" description="Our place in the Union of Messianic Jewish Congregations: Torah covenant faithfulness, Jewish communal life, faith in Yeshua, and mutual support.">
    <div class="editorial-page">
        <section class="editorial-lead" aria-labelledby="umjc-lead-title">
            <div>
                <h2 id="umjc-lead-title">Union of Messianic Jewish Congregations</h2>
                <p><strong>Kehilat Ohr HaTorah</strong> is a member of the Union of Messianic Jewish Congregations (UMJC).</p>
                <p>The UMJC brings congregations together around faith in Yeshua the Messiah and responsibility for Jewish covenant life. Its vision connects Torah, Jewish tradition, and the New Covenant with continuing participation in the life of the Jewish people.</p>
                <a class="text-link" href="https://www.umjc.org/vision" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the UMJC’s vision <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
            <aside class="editorial-side" aria-label="Our congregational identity">
                <ul class="editorial-link-list">
                    <li><a href="/mission#vision-and-purpose">Vision and Purpose <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li>
                    <li><a href="/mission#core-commitments">Core Commitments and Affirmations <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li>
                    <li><a href="/mission#core-values">Core Values <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li>
                </ul>
            </aside>
        </section>
        <section class="editorial-section editorial-split" aria-labelledby="membership-reason">
            <h2 id="membership-reason">Why we belong</h2>
            <div>
                <p class="membership-statement"><IdentityRichText content={umjcMembershipValue} /></p>
                <p>Membership connects our congregation with a wider community of learning, mutual support, and accountability. The union offers education and mentoring for congregational leaders, brings families together at conferences, and helps member communities support one another in times of need.</p>
                <a class="text-link" href="https://www.umjc.org/why-join-the-union" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">How the union serves its congregations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="editorial-section" aria-labelledby="shared-life">
            <h2 id="shared-life">Jewish life in Messiah</h2>
            <div class="editorial-columns">
                <div>
                    <h3 class="icon-heading"><i class="fas fa-scroll editorial-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Torah and covenant faithfulness</span></h3>
                    <p>In the UMJC’s definition, Messianic Judaism shares the Jewish people’s history and covenantal responsibility. Scripture guides this life, while Jewish tradition connects present-day practice with earlier generations. Torah is lived and applied within the New Covenant.</p>
                    <a class="text-link" href="https://www.umjc.org/defining-messianic-judaism" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The UMJC’s definition of Messianic Judaism <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h3 class="icon-heading"><i class="fas fa-people-group editorial-icon" aria-hidden="true"></i><span>Unity and distinct callings</span></h3>
                    <p>The UMJC understands Jewish and non-Jewish followers of Yeshua as united in one Body of Messiah, with their distinct identities and callings preserved. Its vision values a full place within the Jewish people and a relationship of mutual blessing with the wider Christian community.</p>
                    <a class="text-link" href="/mission#core-commitments">Read our congregation’s commitments <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>
        <section class="editorial-section editorial-split">
            <h2>Faith in Yeshua, Israel’s Messiah</h2>
            <div>
                <p>The UMJC’s Statement of Faith affirms God’s enduring covenant with Israel, the authority of the Tanakh and New Covenant writings, and Yeshua’s atoning death and bodily resurrection. It looks forward to his return, the restoration of Israel, and the renewal of creation.</p>
                <p>These convictions belong within the Jewish communal life expressed in our congregation’s own Vision and Purpose, Core Commitments and Affirmations, and Core Values.</p>
                <a class="text-link" href="https://www.umjc.org/statement-of-faith" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the UMJC’s Statement of Faith <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</PageLayout>
